# regexp (step 9.4c): Go's package; makeOnePass drops the reference its recursive closure holds to itself.

@note makeOnePass declares `check` as a variable and assigns a closure that calls `check`. In gocpp a closure that refers to itself through the variable it is stored in is a reference cycle (D1, ADR-004): the closure, the queues and the rune tables it captured were never freed, about 5 KB for every one-pass regexp that was compiled. The patch sets the variable to nil when makeOnePass is done with it.

@file onepass.go
@why The closure `check` captures the variable `check` (it calls itself); setting the variable to nil before makeOnePass returns breaks the cycle, and nothing calls check afterwards.
@replace
	if p != nil {
		for i := range p.Inst {
			p.Inst[i].Rune = onePassRunes[i]
		}
	}
	return p
@with
	if p != nil {
		for i := range p.Inst {
			p.Inst[i].Rune = onePassRunes[i]
		}
	}
	check = nil // the closure calls itself through this variable: a reference cycle in gocpp
	return p
@end
